Reason:
The `loadUserTypes` method iterates over the `udts` collection without checking if it is empty. If `udts` is empty, the loop does not execute, but subsequent code that assumes there are user types to process can lead to runtime errors, as the method does not handle the empty case properly.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```java
if (udts.isEmpty()) {
    return;
}
```
Reason:
This check at the beginning of the `loadUserTypes` method ensures that if the `udts` collection is empty, the method will return immediately without attempting to process any user types, thus preventing runtime errors when loading keyspaces with no user types.

